    "curvature": true,
    "note": "Mount Fuji stands 70 km to the west-north-west (bearing 275 degrees from the Kamakurakokomae crossing), behind Hakone; with Enoshima it is this coast's backdrop. So the land past the frame reaches 80 km here (156 m cells, a 640-line grid) and is lowered by the Earth's curve (far.curvature), which puts Fuji's summit 2.8 degrees over the horizon as it is seen from the beach. Fuji shows on a clear day and not on a hazy one: the haze's distances are stretched (clarity 1.8), a chosen value for the clear air of late autumn and winter, when the mountain is most often seen."
  },
